---
import '~/drag-edges/style.css'
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout title="Lenis Drag Edges">
  <main>
    <section>
      <h1>1. Form controls &amp; selection</h1>
      <p class="expect">
        Expect: dragging inside a field selects its text / moves its control —
        the page must not scroll. Dragging the page elsewhere must not activate
        links or buttons on release.
      </p>
      <div class="cards">
        <div class="card">
          <label>text input — drag to select</label>
          <input type="text" value="drag across this text to select it" />
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <label>textarea — drag-select + resize corner</label>
          <textarea>drag to select, and drag the resize corner</textarea>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <label>range — drag the thumb</label>
          <input type="range" min="0" max="100" />
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <label>select — open and pick</label>
          <select>
            <option>option a</option>
            <option>option b</option>
            <option>option c</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <label>contenteditable — drag to select</label>
          <div contenteditable="true">editable text, drag to select me</div>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <label>click suppression</label>
          <a href="/core">link — click navigates, drag must not</a>
          <button onclick="this.textContent = 'clicked!'">
            button — click fires, drag must not
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <label>video with controls — drag the scrubber</label>
          <video
            controls
            muted
            playsinline
            preload="metadata"
            src="https://interactive-examples.mdn.mozilla.net/media/cc0-videos/flower.mp4"></video>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <label>video without controls — page drag must work here</label>
          <video
            muted
            playsinline
            loop
            autoplay
            preload="metadata"
            src="https://interactive-examples.mdn.mozilla.net/media/cc0-videos/flower.mp4"></video>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <label>audio — drag the scrubber</label>
          <audio
            controls
            preload="metadata"
            src="https://interactive-examples.mdn.mozilla.net/media/cc0-audio/t-rex-roar.mp3"></audio>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <label>draggable — native drag-and-drop must start</label>
          <div class="draggable-chip" draggable="true">
            drag me — expect a drag ghost, not a page scroll
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <label>input inside shadow DOM — drag to select</label>
          <div id="shadow-host"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <label>plain text</label>
          <p>
            page-level selection is the documented tradeoff: with drag enabled,
            dragging here scrolls instead of selecting.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h1>2. Gesture latch (prevent / nested)</h1>
      <p class="expect">
        Expect: a drag keeps the target it started on. Start inside a box and
        leave it — the page must not start scrolling mid-gesture. Start on the
        background and cross a box — the page drag must not freeze.
      </p>
      <div class="cards">
        <div class="scrollbox" data-lenis-prevent>
          <div class="filler">
            data-lenis-prevent — native scroller. Start a drag in here, then
            move the pointer outside.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="scrollbox">
          <div class="filler">
            nested scroller (no prevent). Start a page drag on the background,
            then cross over this box.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h1>3. Iframe crossing</h1>
      <p class="expect">
        Expect: a page drag crossing the iframe keeps tracking (needs pointer
        capture). Also try releasing the button while over the iframe — then
        check the HUD for STUCK.
      </p>
      <iframe
        title="drag-edges iframe"
        srcdoc="<body style='font-family: monospace; padding: 1rem;'><h2>iframe</h2><p>pointer events end here — without capture, a drag freezes while over this area.</p></body>"
      ></iframe>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h1>4. Release outside the window</h1>
      <p class="expect">
        Expect: drag toward the browser chrome / outside the OS window and
        release there, then move the mouse back — the HUD must not show STUCK
        (a stuck state means the missed pointerup left a phantom drag).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h1>5. Pointer types</h1>
      <p class="expect">
        Expect (decision pending): a pen/stylus drag should behave like the
        mouse. The HUD shows the last pointerType — with a pen it currently
        reads "pen" and drag does nothing (only "mouse" is accepted).
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <pre id="hud"></pre>
  <script src="../../drag-edges/test.ts"></script>
</Layout>
